{
  "agent": "holmes-native",
  "artifact_text": "### Observations\n1. In pod `orders-api-7b7dfdc66d-s2556` logs, the readiness probe repeatedly logged `WARN database orders-db-primary.demo-apps.svc:5432 not reachable ([Errno -2] Name or service not known), retrying`.\n2. Kubernetes pod events record 98 consecutive readiness probe failures returning HTTP status code 503 (`Readiness probe failed: HTTP probe failed with statuscode: 503`).\n3. Deployment change log entry `CI-2459` updated ConfigMap `orders-config` setting `DB_HOST` to non-existent Kubernetes service `orders-db-primary.demo-apps.svc:5432` instead of `orders-db`.\n\n### Ruled-out Leads\n1. Pod container crashes or OOM kills were ruled out because the pod status shows `restartCount: 0` and state `Running`.\n2. Node-level scheduling and image pulling issues were ruled out because pod events show `Scheduled`, `Pulled`, and `Started` succeeded immediately.\n\n### Root Cause\nConfigMap `orders-config` was rolled out pointing `DB_HOST` to nonexistent hostname `orders-db-primary.demo-apps.svc:5432`, causing the container's `/ready` TCP database probe to fail with DNS resolution error `[Errno -2] Name or service not known`.\n\n### Recommended Action\nThe orders team should revert ConfigMap `orders-config`'s `DB_HOST` back to `orders-db.demo-apps.svc:5432` and restart the deployment.",
